sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-17> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Xenobots, proto-organisms that form spontaneously from dissociated frog embryo skin cells, are motile via cilia and perform kinematic self-replication, building copies of themselves from loose cells in the medium, a novel solution reached within 48 h without any evolutionary history of selection as Xenobots.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Xenobots perform kinematic self-replication not known in any other species";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Bioelectric networks: the cognitive glue enabling evolutionary scaling from physiology to mind”, Animal cognition (2023), doi:10.1007/s10071-023-01780-3; section “Basal cognition without neurons: what dynamic bodies think about › Creative problem-solving by adaptive morphogenesis: plasticity, not just emergent complexity”. Scope: Xenobots made from Xenopus laevis embryonic ectoderm (Kriegman et al. 2021a)"
}
